  "conclusions": [
    "No mathematical blocker found in the complete 214-line source. It directly imports NativeInterp and reuses the existing quotient/WF semantic construction; no consistency or arithmetic soundness assumption is introduced.",
    "fixed_models takes an externally supplied Nonempty set structure, the six-field ZFAxioms bundle, power sets and regularity. It handles equality plus the seven fixed Foundation ZF axioms. Empty set and Infinity use the bundled induction set and extensionality; union/regularity rearrange the exact existing membership conventions.",
    "In every model of NativeSet.nativeTheory, the quotient WF subtype obtains nonemptiness, the six-field bundle, power and regularity from existing CP/GIC results. This is an external model construction on ordinary Lean types.",
    "models_intF_iff specializes NativeInterp.eval_intF to sentences with empty environments. native_proves_intF and native_proves_domain use ordinary first-order completeness; the latter supplies a representative of a nonempty quotient-WF element. No assumption that the native theory is consistent is needed for these proof conclusions.",
    "emb_intF is an external structural recursion over standard finite formulas with an empty free-variable type. quote_intF_sentence bridges ordinary sentence quotation to InternalInterpretation.interp for PN in an arbitrary IΣ1 model.",
    "provable_domain is uniform over arbitrary arithmetic IΣ1 models W and has exactly the core nonempty-domain premise Provable nativeTheory (^∃ (dom PN)). This conceptually subsumes the earlier uncompiled NativeDomainNonempty scratch draft for the same PN; no duplicate implementation is needed.",
    "provable_interp_fixed is uniform in W but its σ : SetTheorySentence and membership hypothesis σ ∈ EQ ∪ zfFixed are external standard-syntax inputs. It does not itself quantify over arbitrary internal p : W with p ∈ ZF.Δ₁Class and does not supply the full hAx callback."
  ],
  "remaining": [
